           Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================


        The linechat door is a chat door with one window where
        the user and the sysop can type lines one at a time.

        At the beginning of the line there is a prompt with
        the name of the sysop or user .. when a line is
        full the door goes to the next line and starts it
        with a prompt.

        If the sysop or user has just typed something and the
        other party starts to type the door ends the line
        prints an empty line and starts the line with a prompt
        for the other part.

        If a person who is typing types 2 returns something
        similair is happening. The door prints and empty line
        and starts the next line with a prompt for the
        other party.

        Note that the whole chat is logged in a log file in
        the log directory. Including error corrections and
        initials.  Also each chat in the log is started with
        a header with the full name of the chatter.


        Add something like the folowing to your menu
        to use the linechat door.
        The "-" is the character you use to start the chatdoor
        and can be changed to your needs. The "-" character
        is specially chosen to symbolise the single window
        of the linechatter .. together with a "=" for the 
        splitchatter they are easy to remember.



Cmd "-" , 0-255
   CliDoor  "doors:chatdoor/LineChat ~50 "
EndCmd


        Or something like this is you only want the sysop to
        be able to start the Chatdoor.


Cmd "-" , S , 0-255
   CliDoor  "doors:chatdoor/LineChat ~50 "
EndCmd






